#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172131 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171711 :question/id #uuid "fce43073-3f48-5e12-a5c0-ecef3a31a57a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12346" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{S} (x-y)\\: \\textrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx = u+v, \\qquad \ny = u-v, \\qquad \nz = v\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u+v, \\: u-v, \\: v\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =x-y\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)-(u-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 3, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}(x-y)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}2v\\sqrt{6}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}2v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}1\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3}\\cdot [u]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 9\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =27\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540197 :question-generator/id #uuid "c3e9b683-f86b-5dd8-a733-33d6da415377" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186172131.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11345332-1583-5403-b382-1f7db9544110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414431} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed83581-5e32-5a0e-8a25-178bb99cade4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414439} {:answer/id #uuid "7d00c43b-e899-573d-afa8-6b12ead91cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414440} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8100ab-c718-514d-8f3c-f28643c256a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414447} {:answer/id #uuid "d24b3aff-8b91-5bf0-8ab1-f276e0780c98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d00c43b-e899-573d-afa8-6b12ead91cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414440} :answer-field/id #uuid "be382d30-f02e-5329-bcf7-16808280a34b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414459}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82d5af65-9d79-5b70-b0f6-be91c0743951" :question/math-academy-id "q-160834" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(2x+y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u+2,\\hspace{0.222em}u+2v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{70}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{70}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(2x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x=2u-v\\,y=3u+2\\,z=u+2v} \\\\  & =2(2u-v)+(3u+2)+(u+2v) \\\\  & =8u+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(8u+2)\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\,(8u+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8u+2)\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot [4{u}^{2}+2u]_{0}^{1}\\cdot [u]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a1c5c4-aaff-5dad-85ae-7c455c4e77b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169132} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5264d6-51e2-571c-a97d-f200747b780d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169133} {:answer/id #uuid "d262b1ed-6abf-5731-aad7-a59edbd4996a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169134} {:answer/id #uuid "033ce6a7-bfa6-5c47-acc2-cddc0cab717e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169135} {:answer/id #uuid "2814803c-3a0a-59a5-b8f2-9a2b1d57c431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5264d6-51e2-571c-a97d-f200747b780d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169133} :answer-field/id #uuid "126dc10e-27a9-5d7d-894d-84b3d2d7de05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169131}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "588db1ad-67d5-5fad-b786-e13158fbed5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160835" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=6-3u-2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,6-3u-2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =4xy\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=6-3u-2v} \\\\  & =4uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot 4\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =36\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0665e53-645a-508e-8a48-66627b805582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0665e53-645a-508e-8a48-66627b805582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234874} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb05908-2cad-5f19-9002-4431259f7c7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235021}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a131946-3c50-5cb9-8c20-5138d22bf7c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-167649" :question/problem "If we denote our surface of revolution by $S,$ then the total electric charge of the shell is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q={∬}_{S}^{}d(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S=\n$$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nPreviously, we determined that our surface can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\hspace{0.222em}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta ,\\hspace{0.222em}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta ⟩,\\hspace{1em}x\\in [0,1],\\hspace{1em}\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nand the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{x}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{\\theta }^{'}‖=2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(x,\\theta )$ into $d(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(\\mathbf{r}(x,\\theta )) & =\\frac{x({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x((2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta )^{2}+(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta )^{2})}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{5}({\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta )}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}d(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}d(\\mathbf{r}(x,\\theta ))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{x}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{\\theta }^{'}‖\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{4{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}8{x}^{7}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8{x}^{7}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =[{x}^{8}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot [\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "430ab58b-bfb3-5ff3-a26e-50e397241376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276070} {:answer/id #uuid "5ccc6906-339a-55eb-81c6-e1340f0e3809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276304} {:answer/id #uuid "982d058a-fa6a-596f-b4ad-7f3c34706a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276844} {:answer/id #uuid "a9293427-c368-56c5-9cb1-7d5a9b4ac305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277002} {:answer/id #uuid "c4de9476-c71d-52f0-8f43-c4631b831c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ccc6906-339a-55eb-81c6-e1340f0e3809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276304} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a05d06b-9876-5842-ad9e-eec5778c2d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277999}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fb6920aa-28a6-5cb5-a583-f417d82bbe6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161127" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}u,\\hspace{0.222em}v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & ={x}^{2}-2yz\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}-2uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{3}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+u{v}^{2}]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}+2{v}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{2}{3}v+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057c351a-27e3-59d3-8013-345a5bcfa346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275525} {:answer/id #uuid "112a6f37-066f-50c9-88b8-4b14bca55e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275630} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8621e4-8335-55f8-9a71-143f24ae4226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275866} {:answer/id #uuid "61176df2-a86f-5867-9df7-fe03f3d206d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276352} {:answer/id #uuid "61458edd-83a0-5587-a19b-e0a38ccdc25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61458edd-83a0-5587-a19b-e0a38ccdc25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276356} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0ae5ad-a7f1-591f-bc08-e13a68747a2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277844}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3da3d1c-88b2-5b2c-b1c5-adc3acc48bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-161180" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(x+2y-z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u+2v,\\hspace{0.222em}2v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le u\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le 2\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=6.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=6.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(x+2y-z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2u+2v\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =(u-v)+2(2u+2v)-(2v) \\\\  & =5u+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}(5u+v)\\cdot 6\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}(5u+v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{5{u}^{2}}{2}+vu]}_{0}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{5}{2}+v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{[\\frac{5v}{2}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =6[5+2] \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ebe36cd-b1cf-5ce2-8a67-8db3468807b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275603} {:answer/id #uuid "18ad7ac0-5137-5083-9463-529f4f7e3804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275706} {:answer/id #uuid "4891c5fb-95c8-5c1c-a256-07260e4f9797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276121} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ef9b7-1bf5-5710-8957-97f3d292a525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276898} {:answer/id #uuid "c983dee7-7745-56ff-a7b7-c03e844d53b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18ad7ac0-5137-5083-9463-529f4f7e3804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275706} :answer-field/id #uuid "92141582-6640-51e0-ab76-f6c1c7dbae93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277984}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6424aa2-1e21-5507-975b-b73e043b3939" :question/math-academy-id "q-161182" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}6xyz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =6xyz\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =6(u)(u+v)(v) \\\\  & =6({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}6({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}v}{3}+\\frac{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{v}{3}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{v}^{3}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1edff915-88e9-58d6-841c-692c1f2c3ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275757} {:answer/id #uuid "1f390458-0093-558d-b9b3-ca785ff90164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275761} {:answer/id #uuid "63d3f2e3-cd39-56de-8c0d-2c0e4e41eb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276381} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc91682-3c42-5615-aa8f-2f96cb4a6fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277290} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc623d0-26c3-57ab-9f42-45751dbc3aea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d3f2e3-cd39-56de-8c0d-2c0e4e41eb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276381} :answer-field/id #uuid "a91deb21-01ab-5168-9791-852593bfeb6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278017}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "80e5707a-3b53-57aa-aa8c-7db876d69b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-161209" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(xy+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u-v,\\,z=0\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+0+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =xy+z\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u-v\\,z=0} \\\\  & =(u+v)(u-v) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le u\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le v\\le 2\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}(xy+z)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 2\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}-{v}^{2}u]}_{0}^{1}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{v}{3}-\\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}] \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f7d03c6-d0d9-529a-bce7-fcfcb60d6f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276187} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca921c6-81e9-5022-989e-b96d7ae33f08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276453} {:answer/id #uuid "8b30494f-8e6d-5099-9018-d53a7f2a115d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276740} {:answer/id #uuid "b4db6155-6904-59b9-b3a7-494630d4b44a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277090} {:answer/id #uuid "c41eebb1-ad78-5933-9beb-c7c83212c490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4db6155-6904-59b9-b3a7-494630d4b44a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277090} :answer-field/id #uuid "17135030-c131-5443-8329-4345c0e7edd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277766}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aaa6b101-413b-5c8f-a474-bfd4f4726f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161212" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}2xz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=u+v,\\,z=2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\hspace{0.222em}-2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨2,\\hspace{0.222em}-2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =2xz\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =2u(2v) \\\\  & =4uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}2xz\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}4uv\\cdot 3\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}4uv\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}2v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfe6a46-a159-59d8-bee6-18072e5661ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275577} {:answer/id #uuid "5d212cf2-6ea0-53a0-9bcc-5ecd7212b036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276306} {:answer/id #uuid "76f545bd-11b2-5ae1-929d-c2f25977a30f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276549} {:answer/id #uuid "b08aefb8-1f20-592d-9092-298b802a0a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277056} {:answer/id #uuid "b1167d7b-282c-533d-bad4-77099f24e2f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76f545bd-11b2-5ae1-929d-c2f25977a30f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276549} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6564796-0979-5996-bb99-982fadfe08ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278126}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81e32a26-4f8e-507c-9b65-da0df62a940b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161242" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-3v,\\,z=4v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u,\\hspace{0.222em}-3v,\\hspace{0.222em}4v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}-3,\\hspace{0.222em}4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}-8,\\hspace{0.222em}-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}-8,\\hspace{0.222em}-6⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =x(y+z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=2u\\,y=-3v\\,z=4v} \\\\  & =2u(-3v+4v) \\\\  & =2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}2uv\\cdot 10\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}4uv\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}2v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =5\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278443 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "315458db-5834-5453-b924-0dc1201d2a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "102" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275915} {:answer/id #uuid "3f637c5a-3c45-5126-82aa-7a59ac498fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276026} {:answer/id #uuid "62f9e58f-ad46-5445-831b-6ee4a956c58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276373} {:answer/id #uuid "9961fb98-fed5-544f-98af-e57bcc6d74f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276854} {:answer/id #uuid "f811b651-f27c-5a53-a849-08f534196ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f811b651-f27c-5a53-a849-08f534196ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277644} :answer-field/id #uuid "4225a37a-d844-5f27-b52c-36d4f1ac1cc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277828}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c63ddeef-33ef-5328-bfb9-278493d60c61" :question/math-academy-id "q-161245" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}({x}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2u+v,\\,y=2u-2v,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $1\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2,\\hspace{0.222em}2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\hspace{0.222em}-3,\\hspace{0.222em}-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\hspace{0.222em}-3,\\hspace{0.222em}-6⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & ={x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=2u+v\\,y=2u-2v\\,z=u+2v} \\\\  & =(2u+v)^{2}-(u+2v)^{2} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}-1\\le u\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}1\\le v\\le 2\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\cdot 9\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9{∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{u}^{3}-3{v}^{2}u]}_{-1}^{1}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2-6{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9\\cdot [2v-2{v}^{3}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22129875-cc14-5ad3-8bba-b26995c05188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414433} {:answer/id #uuid "38973f90-0f85-5e71-8380-79a67500ceed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414435} {:answer/id #uuid "44291a57-8b30-555c-b7e9-95314ffa4f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414436} {:answer/id #uuid "ab922d47-0766-574c-83bb-4e4ccfbb77ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414444} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fe1620-65f9-5859-8a82-9a5f97b2fafb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1fe1620-65f9-5859-8a82-9a5f97b2fafb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414452} :answer-field/id #uuid "93abc2ba-af03-5472-9cce-10fe847607a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414458}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d27e0ee0-ad93-5416-8abb-f21167765a8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161181" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(3x-2y+3z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}-v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 0\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=2\\sqrt{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(3x-2y+3z)\\,{|}_{x=2u+v\\,y=2u+v\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =3(2u+v)-2(2u+v)+3(-v) \\\\  & =2(u-v)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2(u-v)\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{∬}_{D}\\,(u-v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}u-v\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}-vu]}_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(0-2v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{[-{v}^{2}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b5899eb-77cf-5b34-b910-c93474d97e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414432} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9b5bd3-6406-550a-9325-8fcec12f33ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414438} {:answer/id #uuid "8846a5c5-d563-5056-8e15-64f5e19db2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414441} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5f84da-ca2b-5738-b498-90f08c5871a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414442} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e130f7-33b8-53a2-a94a-0675fb611102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d9b5bd3-6406-550a-9325-8fcec12f33ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414438} :answer-field/id #uuid "831c917a-be0b-5705-bc09-e4bee9b35277" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f95319f6-2e43-511b-ae0d-9608a991c217" :question/math-academy-id "q-161179" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(x+y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}3v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=3\\sqrt{6}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=3\\sqrt{6}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=3v\\,z=2u-v} \\\\  & =(u+v)+(3v)+(2u-v) \\\\  & =3u+3v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(3u+3v)\\cdot 3\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\,(u+v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{0}^{1}u+v\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+vu]}_{0}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}+v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}{[\\frac{v}{2}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10989bff-b98e-51af-bb4a-b28350a226e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418467} {:answer/id #uuid "1687e4a9-1caf-5ff9-a03a-04a61daf8637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418468} {:answer/id #uuid "3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418469} {:answer/id #uuid "60f276b3-36f3-5fbe-9d10-b5fec8b429a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418470} {:answer/id #uuid "b1865271-a8a9-5f44-b938-a958ba7e5f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418469} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec0f1fd-a976-5791-b23e-66968bb1089c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418476}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d41258e7-4727-5661-9adb-26ceb25d76d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161185" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(xy+xz)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}2v,\\hspace{0.222em}6v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=2\\sqrt{10}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xy+xz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=2v\\,z=6v} \\\\  & =(u)(2v)+(u)(6v) \\\\  & =8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8uv\\cdot 2\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}{∬}_{D}\\,uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}({\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u)({\\int }_{0}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}v) \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}\\cdot {[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "592edeca-a58b-598c-b36b-63081f22b737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "592edeca-a58b-598c-b36b-63081f22b737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540185} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5dfdc6-6e25-5817-aa73-4ea414decde1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a0c552d-208d-5647-bd93-a9e5ea76dedb" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨2u+2v,\\,2u-2v,\\,3v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 3$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=2\\sqrt{34}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{34}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(2u+2v)-(2u-2v)=4v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=2\\sqrt{34}\\iint_D 4v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=2\\sqrt{34}\\int_0^{3}4v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{3}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=2\\sqrt{34}[2v^{2}]_0^{3}[u]_0^{3}\\\\&=2\\sqrt{34}(18-0)(3-0)\\\\&=108\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540182} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0cc3a7-0b20-5f18-b1bb-75c69ce02711" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540186}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44e31a62-0afc-5503-b1c7-497ce942e02a" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨3u+v,\\,3u-v,\\,3v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=3\\sqrt{22}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=3\\sqrt{22}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(3u+v)-(3u-v)=2v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}\\iint_D 2v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}\\int_0^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{2}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}[v^{2}]_0^{3}[u]_0^{2}\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}(9-0)(2-0)\\\\&=54\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dac57afd-cb85-5e46-a6c1-819e0317af41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dac57afd-cb85-5e46-a6c1-819e0317af41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540193} :answer-field/id #uuid "954bfe3d-d924-5d77-a50e-3e9051dff6ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "693fafe3-8347-5fad-b5e8-6328dbf9f45e" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨u+3v,\\,u-3v,\\,2v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=2\\sqrt{11}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(u+3v)-(u-3v)=6v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=2\\sqrt{11}\\iint_D 6v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=2\\sqrt{11}\\int_0^{1}6v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{2}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=2\\sqrt{11}[3v^{2}]_0^{1}[u]_0^{2}\\\\&=2\\sqrt{11}(3-0)(2-0)\\\\&=12\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7782f9c-a288-538e-acbc-09a9550c8baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7782f9c-a288-538e-acbc-09a9550c8baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540191} :answer-field/id #uuid "a78d8176-5589-542a-996f-c9de271e00a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a2ff333-cf5b-5cec-a3d0-9589f8fcca8f" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨2u+2v,\\,2u-2v,\\,v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 3$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=6\\sqrt{2}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=6\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(2u+2v)-(2u-2v)=4v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=6\\sqrt{2}\\iint_D 4v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=6\\sqrt{2}\\int_0^{3}4v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{3}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=6\\sqrt{2}[2v^{2}]_0^{3}[u]_0^{3}\\\\&=6\\sqrt{2}(18-0)(3-0)\\\\&=324\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dedbafb9-efaa-590d-8c64-42ea4de83559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedbafb9-efaa-590d-8c64-42ea4de83559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540194} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3118051-1cc0-525f-9156-39a096b94fde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540195}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0840977-4fb8-5c81-83a0-8548ed739ad4" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨u+2v,\\,u-2v,\\,v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=3\\sqrt{2}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(u+2v)-(u-2v)=4v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{2}\\iint_D 4v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{2}\\int_0^{2}4v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{1}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=3\\sqrt{2}[2v^{2}]_0^{2}[u]_0^{1}\\\\&=3\\sqrt{2}(8-0)(1-0)\\\\&=24\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}]}
